SwarSathi - Third-Party Notices
===============================

SwarSathi is an India-first, offline-capable AAC (augmentative and alternative
communication) app. This file lists the third-party components the app depends
on and the licence terms each is offered under. SwarSathi's own source code is
covered by the separate LICENSE file (Apache-2.0); everything else is covered
here.

Top-level rule
--------------

SwarSathi itself is licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Nothing from these
third parties is redistributed inside the APK: each artefact - artwork, voice
model or phonemiser data - is fetched by the user directly from its publisher,
only when they ask for it. The one component linked into the app is the
permissively licensed sherpa-onnx runtime, which is compiled in rather than
downloaded. No third-party artwork or voice is ever shipped with the app, so the
non-commercial and share-alike obligations below stay with the publisher and the
user, not with the app.

